{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "03YZ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0004": "$S_{Zar}$", "MATH_0005": "$S_\\etale$", "MATH_0006": "$(\\Sch/S)_\\tau$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-structure-sheaf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7582b033d0509f542005f3ae6f1ec3eb3a6e7ae418f0e98c3e4c51255962ff6d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8844cbe17a76dda429bcbe44b9fd995f3628b65b8f90268f31cdf62fcc40e9ed", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. The <TEXTITOPEN_0001>structure sheaf<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> of <MATH_0002> is the sheaf of rings\n<MATH_0003>\non any of the sites <MATH_0004>, <MATH_0005>, or <MATH_0006>\ndiscussed above.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:76698d7f000681e55c80478fa79cb3b5e7e7d1dc0ebeaee2af17387e2bbc7a41", "unit_id": "tag:04HS:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03YZ", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{O}_{S_\\etale}$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2bc3e69ea4830da25bcb125cb4583dbce3db61156a404ced184bc0f83a7eaac9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8c98532e69806616a70e6890731376785397b961524f35d6160a36875e14b354", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIf there is some possible confusion as to which site we are working on\nthen we will indicate this by using indices. For example we may use\n<MATH_0001> to stress the fact that we are working on the\nsmall <ACCENT_0001>tale site of <MATH_0002>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ae54a89fba63853b3351779be4983b69bd689baec382e83141a600529fda820b", "unit_id": "tag:03YZ:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "03YZ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\nH_{fppf}^p(X, \\mathbf{G}_a) =\nH_\\etale^p(X, \\mathbf{G}_a) =\nH_{Zar}^p(X, \\mathbf{G}_a) =\nH^p(X, \\mathcal{O}_X)\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$p \\geq 0$", "MATH_0003": "$H^p_{fppf}(X, \\mathcal{O}_X)$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{theorem-zariski-fpqc-quasi-coherent}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-special-case-fpqc-cohomology-quasi-coherent}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6dfed47d696bc675f39738e9e7179ac9747db19c1f785a7317cca4d4470074cb", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cdc76971722a214b40a1f6a7515d0fb780149c1f6091519c4a28b856c17eb341", "source_text": "In the terminology introduced above a special case of\nTheorem <REF_0001>\nis\n<MATH_0001>\nfor all <MATH_0002>. Moreover, we could use the notation\n<MATH_0003> to indicate the cohomology of the\nstructure sheaf on the big fppf site of <MATH_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bb10febba22dddf5989bea87586047776308f5324a41ac138aca30149aa8de3a", "unit_id": "tag:03P6:statement"}
